course: dictionary
lesson: 13059
title: Short forms: Feb
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Feb is a short form, or abbreviation, of February, the second month of the year. People shorten long words when space is small, such as on calendars, forms, timetables and diaries.
explain: «Our club meets on Tuesday 3 Feb.» Feb stands for February, so the club meets on Tuesday 3 February. Read the words around it to check: a date comes after it.
explain: Feb starts with a capital F, just like February does. You may also see it written as «Feb.» with a full stop. Both forms are correct.
fact: Feb is short for February.
fact: February is the second month of the year.
fact: Write it with a capital F: «Feb».
fact: February has 28 days, or 29 days in a leap year.
fact: You may see it written as «Feb.» with a full stop.
exercise: «The party is on Saturday 12 Feb.» What does Feb stand for? | Fashion | Festival | Feather | *February
exercise: Which full month does the short form Feb stand for? | *February | Fern | March | Friday
exercise: Ruby writes her diary date for the second month. Which is correct? | *Feb | feb | FEb | fEB
test: «Her birthday is on 5 Feb.» How many days does February have in a normal year? | 31 | 26 | 30 | *28
test: Which is the short form for February, the second month? | Fed | Mar | *Feb | Fen
exam: The school timetable says «Feb 2026» at the top. What does Feb mean on this timetable? | Festival | *February | Friday | Fabulous
